What the file says about itself:
  The sea-horizon dip MEASURED on the owner's Caussols photo (13 June 2026): joint fit of the camera
  (EXIF focal, heading, tilt, roll) and of the horizon's altitude, the level set by the two near summits.
  fits[0] = central measurement; the others change one decision each. The tab recomputes R from dipArcmin.

Written by `fog build explain` from data/other.json: edit that, not this file.
